# backend runtime/cache
#
# NOT directory-level ignores. This read `backend/storage/framework/` and
# `backend/storage/logs/`, which excluded those directories outright -- and
# with them Laravel's own .gitignore placeholders, the files whose entire
# job is to make the directories exist in a fresh clone. So they did not
# exist there, and a clean checkout had nowhere for Blade to compile into:
# "Please provide a valid cache path". It worked on developer machines
# because artisan had created the directories there months earlier.
#
# Each of those directories carries its own .gitignore ignoring its own
# contents, so nothing runtime becomes tracked. A negation could not fix
# this in place: git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded directory.
backend/storage/framework/phpstan-tmp/
